    (patchDir + "/mpdoutputset-patch.py") # fix bug where `outputset {ID} {NAME} {VALUE}` (MPD 0.24+) was entirely missing from mopidy_mpd 3.3.0 and always ACK unknown command. Newly discovered/reconsidered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent) since all TODO items were consumed (previously shelved as "mopidy's audio output abstraction has no runtime-attribute concept," but it turns out that even in real MPD (OutputCommands.cxx handle_outputset/Interface.cxx AudioOutput::SetAttribute base implementation) an output plugin with no attributes always returns std::invalid_argument("Unsupported attribute") -> ACK_ERROR_ARG(2) as the correct response, which is no reason to leave the command unimplemented). Checked ID validation against CheckPartitionOutput() (OutputCommand.cxx), reuse the existing _mpdoutputpartition_owned() as-is for ID/membership check -> attribute-name char validation (alphanumeric and _ only) -> always return Unsupported attribute (actually changing nothing, a protocol-layer-only pattern like mpdcrossfade-patch.py)
