    (patchDir + "/mpdargvmax-patch.py") # fix bug where mopidy_mpd/tokenize.py's split() set no cap on the total argument-token count per command line. Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent) since all TODO items were consumed. Real MPD (checked src/command/AllCommands.cxx command_process() via gh raw) checks `argv.full()` right before push_back'ing a token to `StaticVector<const char*, COMMAND_ARGV_MAX> argv`, and if exceeded immediately returns ACK Too many arguments (even for an unknown command name) before command_checked_lookup(). COMMAND_ARGV_MAX = 2 + TAG_NUM_OF_ITEM_TYPES*2 (src/tag/Type.hxx, currently 36 tag types) = 74. Since src/client/Response.hxx's command field defaults to an empty string until SetCommand() (called only inside command_checked_lookup()) is called, the ACK at this check point is always `{}` (regardless of whether the command name is known/unknown). Confirmed no prior mention by searching BACKLOG.md/nix/lib/mopidy-env.nix for "ARGV_MAX"/"Too many arguments"/"COMMAND_ARGV_MAX", and that existing patches touching tokenize.py (mpdauthtabsplit/mpdcmdlisttabsplit/mpdcommandnamecase/mpdstrictnumparse/mpdtokenizecommandnone) are all different axes of command-name lexing or the numeric parser and don't handle the token count. Fix: add constant `_MPD_COMMAND_ARGV_MAX = 74` to tokenize.py, and in split()'s while loop, right after a successful PARAM_RE token extraction and just before result.append, add a `len(result) - 1 >= _MPD_COMMAND_ARGV_MAX` check (the same check timing as real MPD's argv.full()). The raised MpdArgError explicitly specifies command="" (same convention as mpdtokenizecommandnone-patch.py; without it, it propagates with command=None without going through dispatcher.py's tokens[0] completion (which works only inside the try block around protocol.commands.call() and doesn't catch split()'s own exceptions), re-triggering the same file's past "{None}" leak bug)
    (patchDir + "/mpdoutputnoopidle-patch.py") # fix bug where enableoutput/disableoutput (audio_output.py) always unconditionally called context.core.mixer.set_mute() even when the requested enable/disable state was already the same as the current mute state (no-op). Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent) since all TODO/known-backlog items were consumed. Real MPD (checked src/output/OutputCommand.cxx audio_output_enable_index()/disable_index() via gh raw) returns true and fires EmitIdle(IDLE_OUTPUT) only when LockSetEnabled(true/false) actually changed the state, and on no state change (no-op) early-returns without firing (confirmed sibling command toggleoutput is out of scope since LockToggleEnabled() always flips the state so there's no no-op concept). The mopidy/audio/actor.py SoftwareMixer.set_mute() the dev environment uses unconditionally calls trigger_mute_changed() regardless of whether the value changed, so mopidy_mpd wrongly fired the changed: output idle notification via mute_changed even when the value didn't change at all. The exact same root cause (SoftwareMixer's unconditional trigger_*_changed) was already fixed for volume (relative) by mpdvolumenoopidle-patch.py, but sibling commands enableoutput/disableoutput (mute direction) were left unhandled. Confirmed the existing items in BACKLOG.md (mpdoutputtogglerace/mpdoutputpartition/mpdidlemixerpartition) cover only race/partition-ownership/cross-partition-idle-leak by searching for "enableoutput"/"disableoutput"/"LockSetEnabled"/"no-op", and this (same-partition no-op idle suppression) has no prior mention. Fix: within the _output_mixer_lock scope mpdoutputtogglerace-patch.py already added, check the current mute state before the set_mute() call and if already matching the requested state treat it as a no-op with success=True (the same "only when actually changed" guard as real MPD's LockSetEnabled())
    (patchDir + "/mpdplayercontrolpartition-patch.py") # fix bug where crossfade/mixrampdb/mixrampdelay (mpdcrossfade-patch.py/mpdmixramp-patch.py) and replay_gain_mode (mpdreplaygain-patch.py) were implemented on translator.py as mere process-wide shared global variables and leaked between multiple partitions made via newpartition (mpdpartition-patch.py). Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent) since all TODO/known-backlog items were consumed. Real MPD (checked src/command/PlayerCommands.cxx handle_crossfade/handle_mixrampdb/handle_mixrampdelay call client.GetPlayerControl().SetXxx(), and src/Partition.hxx holds a PlayerControl independently per partition via gh raw) makes crossfade/mixrampdb/mixrampdelay independent per partition. replay_gain_mode too (checked src/command/PlayerCommands.cxx handle_replay_gain_mode calls partition.SetReplayGainMode(), and src/Partition.hxx's replay_gain_mode is a member of the Partition instance itself via gh raw), and mpdreplaygain-patch.py's introduction comment "real MPD's ReplayGainMode is also process-wide shared" turned out to be wrong, written without checking real MPD source. Confirmed no prior mention by searching BACKLOG.md for crossfade/mixramp/replay_gain/partition combinations — mpdvolumepartition-patch.py/mpdoutputpartition-patch.py/mpdidlemixerpartition-patch.py cover only mixer (volume)/output partition ownership. Fix: change the 4 values to the same "partition-name-keyed dict" method as mpdpartition-patch.py's _session_partition/_output_partition, change each playback.py handler to pass translator.partition_get(id(context.session)) (same pattern as mpdvolumepartition-patch.py), and delete no-longer-needed partition entries from each dict on delpartition (mpdpartitiondeltoctou-patch.py's partition_try_delete()). Confirmed on real hardware (TCP 6601, 2 connections A (default)/B (switched to newpartition zoneX)): after A runs crossfade 15/mixrampdb -10.5/replay_gain_mode track, before, B's status/replay_gain_status leaked xfade:15/mixrampdb:-10.5/replay_gain_mode:track, and after, B's status shows no xfade/mixrampdb lines (treated as 0 and omitted, consistent with mpdxfadezero-patch.py/mpdmixramp-patch.py's existing conditional-output logic) and replay_gain_status stays replay_gain_mode: off unchanged. Also confirmed A's side keeps reflecting the set values (xfade:15/mixrampdb:-10.5/replay_gain_mode:track), a new newpartition zoneX after delpartition zoneX returns to defaults, and 0 new ERROR/Traceback in mopidy.log. Known remaining item (out of scope): the idle "options" notification the above 4-value changes fire is still unconditionally broadcast to all partitions in this patch, and partition-limited delivery like mpdidlemixerpartition-patch.py is left as a separate independent item
    (patchDir + "/mpdcrossfadeidlepartition-patch.py") # resolve the known remaining item mpdplayercontrolpartition-patch.py left: fix bug where the idle "options" notification the changes of crossfade/mixrampdb/mixrampdelay (mpdcrossfadeidle-patch.py)/replay_gain_mode (mpdreplaygain-patch.py) fire was still unconditionally broadcast to all partitions even though the values themselves were already separated into per-partition dicts. Newly started by the self-driving agent from mpdplayercontrolpartition-patch.py's own remaining-item comment since all TODO/known-backlog items were consumed. Re-checked real MPD (gh raw, src/command/PlayerCommands.cxx handle_crossfade/handle_mixrampdb/handle_mixrampdelay/handle_replay_gain_mode), all call partition.EmitIdle(IDLE_OPTIONS) and Partition::EmitIdle is own-partition-limited (the same mechanism mpdidlemixerpartition-patch.py confirmed for mixer/output). repeat/random/single/consume are mopidy core's single shared tracklist values so all-broadcast is still correct (out of scope). Fix: reuse mpdidlemixerpartition-patch.py's direct ProxyCall tell() individual-delivery mechanism, add partition_idle_targets(partition) to translator.py taking an arbitrary partition name, and add a partition argument to playback.py's _mpdcrossfadeidle_notify()/_mpdreplaygain_notify() to individually deliver to only that partition's sessions. Confirmed on real hardware (TCP 6601, 2 connections A (default)/B (dedicated idle subscription after switching to newpartition zoneX)): before, A's crossfade/mixrampdb/mixrampdelay/replay_gain_mode change wrongly woke B from idle options, and after, B doesn't wake and only A does. Regression: repeat/random/single/consume changes still wake both partitions (all-broadcast unchanged), confirmed A/B bidirectionally (reverse too), 0 new ERROR/Traceback in mopidy.log
    (patchDir + "/mpdnewpartitionreplaygain-patch.py") # fix bug where a new partition created via newpartition (mpdpartition-patch.py) always started with replay_gain_mode off, unlike real MPD. Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent) since all TODO/known-backlog items were consumed. Real MPD (checked src/Partition.cxx Partition::Partition(name, src) calls SetReplayGainMode(src.replay_gain_mode), and src/command/PartitionCommands.cxx handle_newpartition() passes the calling client's current partition as src via instance.partitions.emplace_back(name, client.GetPartition()) via gh raw; NEWS ver 0.24.13 also states "copy replay_gain_mode when creating a new partition") copies the source partition's replay_gain_mode on new-partition creation. Meanwhile PlayerControl (holding crossfade/mixrampdb/mixrampdelay) is just newly constructed from config.player each time in the base constructor the same constructor delegates to and doesn't inherit src's runtime state — also confirmed the asymmetric spec where only replay_gain_mode is a copy target. mpdplayercontrolpartition-patch.py dict-ized these 4 values by partition name, but translator.partition_try_create() only does _partitions.append(name) without initializing _replay_gain_mode[name], so it always became the fallback default "off". Confirmed no prior mention by searching BACKLOG.md for "newpartition"/"replay_gain"/"SetReplayGainMode" — the recent mpdplayercontrolpartition-patch.py/mpdcrossfadeidlepartition-patch.py cover only inter-partition value/idle-notification leakage and this (copy omission at creation time) has no prior mention. Fix: extend to partition_try_create(name, source_partition="default"), add _replay_gain_mode[name] = _replay_gain_mode.get(source_partition, "off") within the existing lock scope, and have the newpartition() handler get the calling client's current partition via translator.partition_get(id(context.session)) and pass it as source_partition (crossfade/mixrampdb/mixrampdelay stay default and unchanged like real MPD)
    (patchDir + "/mpdbinarylimitmax-patch.py") # fix bug where `binarylimit {SIZE}` (introduced by mpdbinarylimitargerr-patch.py) had none of the command-specific upper-bound check that real MPD's (checked src/command/ClientCommands.cxx handle_binary_limit() via gh raw) `args.ParseUnsigned(0, client.GetOutputMaxSize() - 4096)` has. Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent) since all TODO items were consumed. Based on real MPD's default `client_max_output_buffer_size` (8192*1024 bytes, src/client/Config.cxx), the actual upper bound is 8,384,512, far smaller than protocol.UINT's generic upper bound 0xFFFFFFFF (mpduintmax-patch.py), so values in between (8,384,513 to 4,294,967,295) that should be ACK "Number too large" were silently OK. Confirmed no prior mention by searching BACKLOG.md for "8384512"/"client_max_output_buffer_size"/"GetOutputMaxSize". Fix: add `_MPD_BINARYLIMIT_MAX = 8192 * 1024 - 4096` as a module-level constant and ACK exceptions.MpdArgError("Number too large") when the limit is exceeded, same convention as the existing "Value too small"
    (patchDir + "/mpdplchangesrange-patch.py") # fix bug where `plchanges`/`plchangesposid` (mopidy_mpd/protocol/current_playlist.py) didn't accept the optional `[START:END]` range argument added in MPD 0.20+ at all and ACKed `wrong number of arguments`. Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent) since all TODO items were consumed. Real MPD (checked src/command/QueueCommands.cxx handle_plchanges()/handle_plchangesposid() via gh raw) accepts an optional Range via `args.ParseOptional(1, RangeArg::All())`, and `playlist_print_changes_info/_position` (src/PlaylistPrint.cxx) does `range.ClipRelaxed(queue.GetLength())` (src/protocol/RangeArg.hxx, silently clamps end to length and start to end by the excess without ACKing) then `queue_print_changes_info/_position` (src/queue/Print.cxx) excludes out-of-range positions from iteration entirely via `for (i=start;i<end;i++) if (queue.IsNewerAtPosition(i, version))`. mopidy_mpd originally accepted only the 1 `version` argument, and any 3rd+ token made the dispatcher's argument binding a TypeError and ACK, making range spec itself impossible. Confirmed no prior mention by searching BACKLOG.md for "plchanges"/"START:END"/"RangeArg" (the existing patches touching plchanges/plchangesposid are all only version-comparison logic like TOCTOU races/future-version decisions and don't handle the range argument). Fix: add `songrange=protocol.RANGE` (default `slice(0, None)`=all, same convention as listplaylistinfo) to both commands, do a real-MPD-ClipRelaxed-equivalent clamp with the shared helper `_mpd_plchanges_clip_range()`, delegate the all-songs-return branch to `translator.tracks_to_mpd_format(..., start=, end=)`, and have the single-song (metadata-update/fallback) branch and plchangesposid's enumerate loop return nothing if the target position is out of range
    (patchDir + "/mpdplchangesnoneguard-patch.py") # fix a regression where, inside the retry loop of the version-match (metadata-update-only) branch of plchanges introduced by mpdplchangesrange-patch.py, the range check `if not (start <= position < end):` didn't guard position=None, so when position becomes None in a TOCTOU race (another connection deletes a track between get_current_tl_track() and tracklist.index()), an uncaught TypeError (int <= NoneType comparison) is raised and the whole TCP connection can be disconnected. Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via a 2-stage delegated investigation to a general-purpose subagent, starting from the point-70/mpdmountorder-patch.py-style pattern where "a compound-change patch breaks existing logic's assumptions") since all TODO/known-backlog items were consumed. The same function's post-loop fallback branch already has the correct guard `if position is None or not (start <= position < end):` (added by mpdplchangesrange-patch.py itself), and only the in-loop branch lacked the same guard — an asymmetry. In the old implementation (range-argument-unsupported version) this branch didn't go through the comparison and directly called translator.track_to_mpd_format(tl_track, ..., position=position, ...) where position=None was silently allowed (only Pos:/Id: missing), so this `TypeError` is judged a regression newly introduced by the range patch. Fix: add the exact same `position is None or` guard as the fallback branch to the in-loop branch too
    (patchDir + "/mpdchannelsidlepartition-patch.py") # fix bug where the idle "subscription" notification subscribe/unsubscribe (mpdchannels-patch.py) fire was still the unconditional all-partition broadcast via `_mpdchannels_notify("subscription")` = `mopidy.listener.send(MpdSession, ...)` and unhandled. mpdchannels-patch.py's own comment stated "idle \"subscription\", like real MPD's idle_add(IDLE_SUBSCRIPTION), is correctly an unconditional broadcast to all sessions," but that was a misread of real MPD source. Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent) since all TODO/known-backlog items were consumed. Real MPD (checked src/client/Subscribe.cxx Client::Subscribe()/Client::Unsubscribe() via gh raw) both call `partition->EmitIdle(IDLE_SUBSCRIPTION)`, and Partition::EmitIdle is own-partition-limited (the same mechanism mpdidlemixerpartition-patch.py/mpdcrossfadeidlepartition-patch.py already confirmed for mixer/output/options; distinct from the truly-global idle_add() (src/Idle.cxx), and IDLE_SUBSCRIPTION is unused on the idle_add() side). Confirmed by searching BACKLOG.md for "IDLE_SUBSCRIPTION"/"subscription.*partition"/"_mpdchannels_notify" that there's no prior mention other than mpdchannelpartition-patch.py (which targets only channels/sendmessage subscription-data visibility, with its self-comment explicitly stating idle-notification delivery scope is out of scope). Fix: no new helper needed; just combine mpdcrossfadeidlepartition-patch.py's established translator.partition_idle_targets(partition) with mpdchannels-patch.py's own _mpdchannels_notify_targeted() (pykka ProxyCall direct tell() individual delivery) to replace subscribe()/unsubscribe()'s _mpdchannels_notify("subscription") with individual delivery to only the firing session's partition
    (patchDir + "/mpdsavecreatedefault-patch.py") # fix bug where the MODE-omitted default of `save {NAME} [MODE]` mpdversion-patch.py implemented stayed the old mopidy behavior "create if absent, overwrite if present", inconsistent with real MPD (MODE-omitted is treated as create and rejects if existing). Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent + 2 stages of additional deep-dive) since all TODO/known-backlog items were consumed. mpdversion-patch.py's own comment stated "don't follow real MPD spec to avoid regressing old rmpc calls / save behavior verified in past backlog," but that was a judgment written without verifying how rmpc (mierak/rmpc) actually uses MODE-omitted save. Confirmed by actually cloning: rmpc calls MODE-omitted save_queue_as_playlist in all 3 places — queue.rs "Save queue as playlist", command.rs `rmpc save`, shared/mpd_client_ext.rs create_playlist() (a workaround creating anew via save->playlistclear->add to bypass the inability to create an empty playlist) — all implicitly depending on real MPD's "reject if existing" safety. Real MPD (checked src/command/PlaylistCommands.cxx handle_save(): `PlaylistSaveMode mode = PlaylistSaveMode::CREATE;` is the MODE-omitted default, and src/PlaylistSave.cxx spl_save_queue() throws `PlaylistError(PlaylistResult::LIST_EXISTS, "Playlist already exists")` in CREATE mode if `FileExists()` via gh raw). Real harm: entering an existing playlist name in rmpc's "Save" context menu, save (MODE-omitted) overwrites with the current queue with no warning or ACK, and the following playlistclear+add completely erases the original saved content. Fix: change a 1-line conditional (`mode == "create"` -> `mode in ("create", None)`) to treat MODE-omitted the same as "create" (`ACK Playlist already exists` if existing), and also fix the docstring that described the old premise
    (patchDir + "/mpdplaylistclearguard-patch.py") # fix bug where `playlistclear {NAME}`, when the target playlist doesn't exist, silently created it anew and returned OK, unlike real MPD. Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent) since all TODO items were consumed. mpdplaylistcreateguard-patch.py already fixed the connection disconnect from the unchecked playlists.create() None return (creation failure) at the same place, but the "create anew if absent" path itself had never had its real-MPD conformance checked as existing spec. Real MPD (checked src/command/PlaylistCommands.cxx handle_playlistclear() via gh raw) calls spl_clear(name), and src/PlaylistFile.cxx spl_clear() tries TruncateFile (no O_CREAT) and throws PlaylistError(NO_SUCH_LIST, "No such playlist") if the file is absent (doesn't create). Confirmed an intentional asymmetry: doc/protocol.rst states creation for the playlistadd item but not for playlistclear right below it. Real harm: playlistclear to a nonexistent playlist name silently creates an empty new playlist with no ACK/warning. Fix: remove `_get_playlist(context, name, must_exist=False)` + `playlists.create()` fallback and replace with the same `_get_playlist(context, name)` (must_exist=True default, raises MpdNoExistError) as other sibling commands (listplaylist/rm etc.), and remove the docstring's "created if absent" statement
    (patchDir + "/mpdaddedunify-patch.py") # fix bug where mpdadded-patch.py (in-queue Added, tlid-keyed _queue_added, new timestamp on each add) and mpdlibraryadded-patch.py (out-of-queue Added, uri-keyed _library_added, immutable within a session) looked at two completely independent volatile-store systems for the same track depending on the reference path, so even the same song (same uri) had differing Added values via find/search vs via the queue and the value changed on each queue add/remove. mpdlibraryadded-patch.py's own comment was aware of it but left it unfixed (a recurrence of the pattern where an existing comment is not proof of verification). Newly discovered by the self-driving agent (via delegating investigation to a general-purpose subagent) since all TODO items were consumed. Real MPD's Queue::Item struct (checked src/queue/Queue.hxx via gh raw) has only id/song/version/priority and no Added-equivalent field at all — real MPD has no concept of a "queue add time" (per src/song/DetachedSong.hxx's comment, it just reuses the song-specific DB registration time regardless of path). rmpc's (mierak/rmpc) SongProperty::Added() is referenced with identical semantics from dir_or_song.rs's CmpByProp::cmp() in the queue/search-result/tag-browser/stored-playlist panes alike, so real-machine verification (an Added seen via addid->playlistinfo changing to a different value when the same uri is re-addid'd after delete) confirmed the real harm of unstable sort order. Fix: unify track_to_mpd_format()'s queue-branch Added fetch from tlid-keyed get_added() to uri-keyed get_or_stamp_library_added() (other files unchanged since leaving the write paths does no harm)
