    (patchDir + "/lbmbidartistcredit-patch.py") # fix bug where _collect_playlist_tracks()'s get_recording_by_id(includes=["artists"]) specified the wrong include (for artist-relation), so artist-credit-phrase was effectively always missing from the upstream MusicBrainz API response and the immediately following mb_recording["artist-credit-phrase"] bare-index access unconditionally raised KeyError, causing an actor crash / permanent weekly-re-import stall (change to the correct include "artist-credits" + switch recording/artist-credit-phrase/title to .get())
    (patchDir + "/lbnetguard-patch.py") # fix bug where validate_token()/submit_listen()/list_playlists_created_for_user()/_collect_playlist_data(), while all protecting check_response_status() (non-200 response) with try/except, left the self.session.get()/post() before it defenseless against network-layer errors (requests.exceptions.RequestException: connection refused/timeout etc.), causing an actor crash / permanent weekly-re-import stall
    (patchDir + "/lbtokennetguard-patch.py") # fix bug where Listenbrainz.__init__() misjudged validate_token()'s False return (which after lbnetguard-patch.py also returns False on network-layer errors) as "the token is truly invalid" and raised RuntimeError, crashing the actor via an uncaught on_start() exception and disabling ListenBrainz integration for the process's lifetime (make validate_token()'s return Optional[bool] and return None when undecidable, relaxing to a warning only; fail-fast as before if truly invalid)
    (patchDir + "/lbjsonguard-patch.py") # fix bug where validate_token()/list_playlists_created_for_user()/_collect_playlist_data() defenselessly called response.json() (right after check_response_status()) outside the try block, so even on a 200 response with a non-JSON body (an HTML error page etc.) a JSONDecodeError (a RequestException subclass, but not caught by the existing except since the call site is outside try) slipped through and caused an actor crash / permanent weekly-re-import stall (move response.json() to right after check_response_status() inside try to be caught by the existing except)
    (patchDir + "/lbartistnameguard-patch.py") # fix bug where frontend.py's track_playback_started()/track_playback_ended() unconditionally treated artist names as strings via `", ".join(sorted([a.name for a in track.artists]))`, so a track containing an Artist(name=None) (mopidy.models.Field allows None, and can actually happen since several artist-dict assembly places in mopidy_ytmusic pass through with default-less `.get`) raised TypeError, and the pykka actor permanently stalled as an exception inside a reply_to-less "tell" message, disabling all ListenBrainz integration (exclude name=None artists from sorted/join, the same defense as current_playlist.py's _pf_field_values())
    (patchDir + "/lbplaylistrefresh-patch.py") # fix bug where ListenbrainzPlaylistsProvider.save() decided saving of recommendation (Weekly Jams/Weekly Exploration) playlists by "whether the song count strictly increased from last time," so since ListenBrainz's weekly recommendations keep a nearly fixed song count (50 songs) with only the contents fully replaced, it was almost always ignored from the 2nd week on and the rmpc/mopidy-side playlist was permanently frozen at the first-save song order (change song-count comparison to song-composition (URI sequence, including order) comparison)
    (patchDir + "/lbgetitems-patch.py") # fix bug where ListenbrainzPlaylistsProvider.get_items(), against the PlaylistsProvider contract (return Ref.track for songs within the playlist), returned the matched playlist itself as Ref.playlist as-is (unify to return found[0].tracks as Ref.track like mopidy_ytmusic's get_items())
    (patchDir + "/lbimportobsolete-patch.py") # fix bug where ListenbrainzFrontend.import_playlists() could wrongly obsolete-delete a recommendation playlist confirmed to still exist on the LB side. Since _collect_playlist_data() already excludes playlists with empty track_mbids, tracks==0 on the import_playlists() side isn't because there's no data on the LB side but merely the result of _collect_playlist_tracks()'s local search / MusicBrainz fallback search all failing for that one round, and since the existing decision (pop() from filtered_existing_playlists) was after the tracks==0 continue, it wasn't excluded from deletion candidates and was silently deleted (move pop() before the tracks==0 check)
    (patchDir + "/lbstarttimestamp-patch.py") # fix bug where the listened_at sent to submit_listen() never used self.last_start_time (the song's playback start time) recorded by track_playback_started() and was always the time.time() at the submit_listen() call = track_playback_ended() fire time (the song's playback completion time, further delayed if paused). Against the ListenBrainz submit-listens API spec (listened_at is the playback start time), listened_at was systematically shifted into the future from the actual for all songs (add a listened_at argument to submit_listen() and pass self.last_start_time from track_playback_ended())
  ];
